### PageTurn Library API requests
### 1. In VS Code, install the "REST Client" extension if it is not installed.
### 2. Open a terminal in the PageTurnLibrary folder and run: npm start
### 3. Wait for "Server running at http://localhost:3000".


### 4. Click "Send Request" above any request below to see its status and data.
### Tip: Send the requests in order. The book created below is used for update/delete,
### and the new loan can be used to try the PATCH status flow.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@bookId = {{createBook.response.body.bookId}}
@loanId = {{createLoan.response.body.loanId}}

### Requirement 1: Express server / check that the API is running
### Expected: 200 OK, with the API name and route list in the response panel.
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Requirement 2: SQLite data / view all readers
### Expected: 200 OK, a JSON array with the sample readers from the SQLite database.
GET {{baseUrl}}/readers

### View one reader
### Expected: 200 OK, one reader object (for example Ravi).
GET {{baseUrl}}/readers/1

### Add a reader
### Expected: 201 Created, a new readerId, and a success message.
# @name createReader
POST {{baseUrl}}/readers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pawan Kalyan",
  "email": "pawan@example.com"
}

### Requirement 3: Book CRUD / view all books
### Expected: 200 OK, a JSON array of books.
GET {{baseUrl}}/books

### View one book
### Expected: 200 OK, one book object.
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/1

### Create a book (REST Client automatically uses its returned ID for update/delete)
### Expected: 201 Created, a bookId, and a success message.
# @name createBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Harry Potter",
  "genre": "Fantasy"
}

### Update book with ID in @bookId
### Expected: 200 OK and "Book updated successfully".
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Harry Potter - Updated",
  "genre": "Fantasy"
}

### Delete book with ID in @bookId (only succeeds if no loan uses it)
### Expected: 200 OK if there are no loans for that book; otherwise 409 Conflict.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/{{bookId}}

### Requirement 4: JOIN endpoint / see loan details with reader and book names
### Expected: 200 OK, a JSON array with loan_id, reader_name, book_name, and status.
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans/details

### Requirement 5: Book validation / try an invalid book (expected 400)
### Expected: 400 Bad Request with {"error":"Book name is required"}.
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "cfg",
  "genre": "Science"
}

### Requirement 5: Also test validation when updating a book (expected 400)
### Book 1 exists; the empty name should be rejected before it is updated.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": " ",
  "genre": "Science"
}

### Requirement 6: Search books by genre
### Expected: 200 OK, only books whose genre matches Science.
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?genre=Science

### Loans / list loan records
### Expected: 200 OK, a JSON array of loans and their statuses.
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans

### View one loan
### Expected: 200 OK, one loan object with reader_id, book_id, and status.
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans/1

### Create a loan (starts pending; REST Client automatically uses its returned ID below)
### Expected: 201 Created and a new loanId with status "pending".
# @name createLoan
POST {{baseUrl}}/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reader_id": 1,
  "book_id": 2
}

### Special twist test 1: a new loan starts pending; pending -> done skips a step (expected 400)
### Expected: 400 Bad Request. Send this first, while the new loan is still pending.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/loans/{{loanId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "done"
}

### Special twist test 2: pending -> approved (expected 200)
### Expected: 200 OK and status "approved".
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/loans/{{loanId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "approved"
}

### Special twist test 3: approved -> pending moves backward (expected 400)
### Expected: 400 Bad Request with {"error":"Invalid status change"}.
### The rejected request leaves the new loan approved.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/loans/{{loanId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "pending"
}

### Complete the flow: approved -> done (expected 200)
### Send after the approved -> pending test above.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/loans/{{loanId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "done"
}

### See all current loan data after changes
### Expected: 200 OK; verify the updated loan status in this response.
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans/details
